.
the experience that you get for killing a unicorn is nowhere near
commensurate with the luck penalty, don't do it!!!

unicorns not of your alignment will attack you if given a chance. you
must have been playing as a neutral or chaotic character at the time
that you stoned the white unicorn. imagine the unicorns confusion given
the fact that it intends to do you in and you are generously throwing
(possibly) valuable gems at it. my guess is you pacified it (not tamed)
so it won't do you in but i don't think your luck improved any. the
results are somewhat different for stoning unicorns of your alignment:
white = lawful        gray  = neutral        black = chaotic.

miscellania:
glowing hands: are the mark of a sensitive character (ref. ring of warning).
i haven't completely deciphered (if possible) the different colors but
my guess is that they correspond to proximity to various monster types.
it used to be that warning told you of the creation of new monsters on
your level but i'm not convinced that that rule still applies in nh3.0h6.

polymorph other wands into traps: violates the spirit of polymorph to me.
blessed wands aimed at the ground seemed appropriate for trap creation.

the healers scalpel ought to be a truly surgical instrument as in:
wielded as a weapon it should _only_ do 1 or 2 hit points worth of damage
for a fairly skilled and dexterous character. lower skilled and undexterous
characters would do more damage with a scalpel. i think this has an ironic
benefit for mid-game play.

assuming that the healers new scalpel will generate lots of corpses, it
should, when applied as a tool to a corpse, dissect a piece of that corpse
for later consumption along the lines of the tinning kit but perhaps
taking a few more moves (as the tinning kit is automated but cumbersome).
the dissected zruty corpse, for example, would timeout as do natural
corpses but would only take one move to digest if eaten.

